      "decision": "Fixed before the run (2026-10-15). Main comparison: on the cue phrase (layers 24-40), per lens, in the questions whose two swaps overlap at least the median (cosine of the pairs' difference vectors, as in run 20261015-111137's overlap split) and in all questions, the pinned bridge swap vs the pinned answer swap (paired bootstrap 95% CI). \"Bridge\" if the pinned bridge swap flips more (CI above 0) and stays well above its null: the cue phrase carries the bridge. \"Answer\" if the pinned answer swap flips more: it carries the answer. \"Not separable along these directions\" if both fall near their nulls. Conditions: the plain swaps reproduce the earlier run; the pinned answer swap's positive control (last token, layers 40-56) flips at least 30%, else a low pinned-answer rate on the cue phrase says nothing; and a pinned swap whose median edit is under half its plain swap's is read as weakened by dose, not by content.",
